    "media:imagetext": "years of residence in Hongkong and India he has become an English citizen, married\na most attractive White Russian refugee from Tientsin and seems quite content.\nWe left Delhi late at night on the l4th passed through Calcutta and arrived Bangkok\nearly in the morning of Wednesday October 15th. So leaving New York at 7 PM Sunday\nLosing 12 hours by flying east, I still arrived half way around the world too early\nfor breakfast on Wednesdey morning.\nWe were a little disappointed in Bangkok. Perhaps it wes because the Hotel\nTrocadero was a little more\nshabby and nothing worked with a greater degree of\nregularity than formerly. Perhaps it was because the streets were full of mud in\naddition to their customary disrepair. Maybe it was because the night noises were\nnearer a 100% din than erstwhile. Whatever it was we left this morning with no\nregrets and the firm conviction shared by most visitors that Bangkok needs a first\nclass hotel.\nOn the more constructive side Siam is prosperous, their budget is balanced, their\ngold reserve is 100% of paper currency outstanding. The people have plenty of food\nand there seems little danger of Communism from within. A large group of American\nofficers are training the Thai (Sian) army and air force but most seem to feel that\nSiam will put up little resistance should the Chinese Communists sweep through\nIndo China and overrun the country. They individually seem to share the view held\nby many of China's Nationalist soldiers that if your country is any good its worth\nliving for. We plan to spend this Friday afternoon Saturday end Sunday in Hongkong\nthen on Monday take off for Tokyo.\nlater - Iokyo - Tuesday, October 21st.\nWe had a wonderful time in Hongkong. Max Polin, George Sellett and Jerry 0'Donnell\nmet us at the airport. We all went to a cocktail party given by a prominent\nChinese for an old China Hand named Neil Starr and there met many old friends\nincluding lots of refugees from Shanghai. Later we had dinner at Jerry's home high\nup on the hills overlooking Repulse Bay. The next day Saturday, October 18th,\nwe did some shopping, called on old friends and had dinner at a Chinese restaurant",
